    "created_at": "2023-07-10T22:25:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-10T22:25:27Z",
    "body": "Looking at “the ContextJ rules”, https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5892.html#appendix-A processes a label with a pseudo-code loop of `For All Characters`. On an empty label, this is an empty loop.\r\n\r\nFor CheckBidi, I see that [IDNA2008 appears to trigger the rule](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5891.html#section-4.2.3.4) only if the *label* contains RTL characters while UTS46 triggers it if the *domain name* contains RTL. (Although https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5893.html#section-2 says that it “applies to labels in Bidi domain names”.)\r\nAnd https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5893.html#section-2 just has “1. The first character must be ...”\r\n\r\nIt seems like we could clarify this in UTS46 with this insertion:\r\n> If CheckBidi, and if the domain name is a  Bidi domain name, <ins>and if the label is not empty,</ins> then the label must satisfy ...",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
